course: dictionary
lesson: 12159
title: Following rules with compliance
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Compliance is a formal word, and it means obeying a rule, a law, a request or an order. You will meet it in school notices, safety signs and exam texts. «The school checks that every class is in compliance with the fire safety rules.» Here compliance tells you the classes follow the rules.
explain: The word can also describe a habit. Some people do what others want, sometimes too easily. «His compliance meant he agreed to everything the bully said, even when it was wrong.» Here compliance is not praise. It shows that he gave in without thinking.
explain: Look at the words around compliance to work out which meaning fits. Words like «rule», «law» and «safety» point to the first meaning. Words like «agreed» and «even when it was wrong» point to the second. Then swap in a simpler word, such as «obeying» or «giving in», and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Compliance is a noun, and it is uncountable, so we say compliance, not compliances.
fact: Compliance means obeying a rule, law, request or order.
fact: Useful phrases: in compliance with, compliance with the law, safety compliance.
fact: «In compliance with» means following a rule: «The shop worked in compliance with the law.»
fact: Compliance can also mean doing what other people want, sometimes too easily, so a reader must look at the context to be sure which meaning is meant.
exercise: «The shop was fined because it was not in compliance with the law.» What does compliance with the law mean? | *Obeying the law | Writing new laws for the town | Reading a law book | Breaking the law on purpose
exercise: «Her compliance with the safety rules was excellent.» What does compliance mean here? | Forgetting the rules at lunch | Making up new safety rules | *Following the safety rules | Breaking the windows
exercise: «His compliance meant he agreed to everything the bully said, even when it was wrong.» What does compliance suggest? | Standing up calmly for what is right | Forgetting the rules | *Doing what others want too easily | Being very loud and angry
test: Which phrase means following a rule? | in the middle of | *in compliance with | in charge of | in trouble with
test: In «safety compliance», what does compliance mean? | A new kind of safety equipment | A long safety speech | *Following safety rules | Ignoring safety signs
exam: Which sentence uses compliance in the sense of doing what others want too easily? | The council checked the factory for safety compliance | *He never questioned anyone, he just did whatever the group wanted | The bank changed its rules in compliance with the new law | The fire drill went smoothly because every pupil followed the rules
